{
  "summary": "The FinanceMate UI largely follows the design tokens and navigation flow, but several critical gaps prevent the app from meeting the DESIGN.md spec. The sign‑up/in screens are not accessible (email/password inputs lack proper labels and ARIA attributes), causing the primary flow automation to fail. Dashboard does not handle API‑error, offline, or pull‑to‑refresh states. Receipt capture, mileage entry, and export screens miss required permission UI, loading overlays, and toast feedback. Accessibility roles for the tab bar and header are missing, and the layout does not enforce the 360 px max‑width on mobile or the 720 px pane on desktop. These issues are high‑severity because they break the core user journey and leave defined states unimplemented. Medium‑severity concerns include missing desktop navigation drawer, missing password‑show toggle, live rule helper, and missing autocomplete. Low‑severity items are minor style inconsistencies.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Email and password inputs are rendered without a visible label linked via `accessibilityLabel`/`nativeID` and lack `autoComplete` attributes, causing automated tests to time out and screen readers to announce nothing.",
      "fix": "Add a `<Text>` label above each `<TextInput>` and set `nativeID` on the input. Pass `accessibilityLabel` that matches the visible label (e.g., \"Email address\"), add `autoComplete=\"email\"` and `autoComplete=\"current-password\"`. Link the label with `accessibilityLabelledBy` or `aria-labelledby` for web."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Same accessibility problem as SignUp – email/password fields are not properly labelled, making the sign‑in form inaccessible and breaking flow automation.",
      "fix": "Implement the same labelled input pattern as in SignUpScreen, plus add a \"Forgot password\" link with appropriate role."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "API error and offline states defined in DESIGN.md are not rendered; there is no banner for \"Failed to load data. Pull down to retry.\" or \"You’re offline – data may be outdated.\" and no pull‑to‑refresh handling.",
      "fix": "Add a banner component that displays the error/offline message based on network status. Wrap the `<ScrollView>` with `RefreshControl` to allow pull‑to‑retry. Show the banner when the fetch throws or when `NetInfo` reports offline."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing permission prompt modal, fallback UI when permission is denied, upload loading overlay, and success/error toasts. The spec requires a modal with \"Allow\"/\"Deny\" and a fallback \"Choose from library\" button.",
      "fix": "Use `Modal` to show the permission prompt with the exact copy. On denial, render a view with the fallback notice and button. Wrap the image upload call with `LoadingOverlay` showing \"Uploading receipt…\". After success/failure, fire a toast component with the exact messages."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "No loading overlay while saving mileage, and no toast notifications for success or error. The spec defines a disabled state and spinner overlay with \"Saving mileage…\".",
      "fix": "During the POST request, disable inputs and show `<LoadingOverlay message=\"Saving mileage…\"/>`. On response, display a toast with \"Mileage entry saved.\" or \"Failed to save mileage. Please try again.\""
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export buttons never become disabled during generation, no spinner, and offline export is not blocked. The spec requires disabled buttons with spinner and an offline banner.",
      "fix": "Track export state (`exportingCsv`, `exportingPdf`). While true, set `disabled` on both buttons and render an `ActivityIndicator` inside the button with the appropriate copy (\"Generating CSV…\" / \"Generating PDF…\"). Detect offline via `NetInfo` and show a banner \"Cannot export while offline.\"."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "Header is a plain `<View>` without `SafeAreaView` and only has `accessibilityRole=\"header\"` but no `banner` landmark. On iOS the status bar may overlap and screen readers lose context.",
      "fix": "Wrap the header in `<SafeAreaView edges={['top']}>` and set `accessibilityRole=\"banner\"`. Ensure proper padding for notch devices."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button visual feedback for the pressed (active) state is missing; spec requires background `primaryVariant` on press. Only focus style is defined.",
      "fix": "Replace `TouchableOpacity` with `Pressable` and provide a `style` function that returns `backgroundColor: pressed ? theme.colors.primaryVariant : theme.colors.primary`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Accessibility focus ring is added on `onFocus`, but keyboard navigation on web does not transfer focus to the button (e.g., missing `tabIndex`).",
      "fix": "Add `tabIndex={0}` to the button to make it focusable on web and ensure the focus ring appears with the existing style."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Layout does not enforce the 360 px max‑content width for mobile or center the content on larger screens.",
      "fix": "Wrap the `<ScrollView>` content in a `<View style={{ maxWidth: 360, alignSelf: 'center', width: '100%' }}>` and add a media query or use `Dimensions` to apply a 720 px max‑width for web/desktop."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/App.tsx",
      "issue": "Desktop navigation drawer described in the spec is not implemented; the app only hides the tab bar on web but provides no left drawer.",
      "fix": "Create a `DrawerNavigator` using `@react-navigation/drawer` for the desktop layout, conditionally render it when `Platform.OS === 'web' && Dimensions.get('window').width >= 1280` and populate it with navigation items."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Password field lacks a show/hide eye icon and accessible label \"Show password\". Live password rule list is not displayed.",
      "fix": "Add an eye icon button inside the password input that toggles `secureTextEntry`. Set `accessibilityLabel=\"Show password\"` (and \"Hide password\" when toggled). Below the field, render a `<Text>` with the rule helper: \"12 + characters, upper‑case, lower‑case, number, symbol\"."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Password field also missing show/hide toggle and autocomplete for email/password.",
      "fix": "Add eye-icon toggle and set `autoComplete=\"current-password\"` on the password input; set `autoComplete=\"email\"` on the email input."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/BottomTabBar.tsx (implicit)",
      "issue": "The TabBar does not expose ARIA roles (`tablist`, `tab`) on web, preventing keyboard users from understanding the navigation group.",
      "fix": "Wrap the tab bar in a view with `accessibilityRole=\"tablist\"` and set each tab button `accessibilityRole=\"tab\"` plus `accessibilityState={{ selected: isFocused }}`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/LoadingOverlay.tsx",
      "issue": "Overlay background uses `theme.colors.disabledBackground` (solid) instead of a semi‑transparent overlay as per typical design patterns.",
      "fix": "Change `backgroundColor` to `rgba(0,0,0,0.4)` or use a token for overlay opacity if defined."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button height and min‑width match spec, but the font size is taken from `theme.typography.button` which is 16 px, correct; however the contrast ratio for disabled button (grey on grey) may be low.",
      "fix": "Confirm that `theme.colors.disabled` on `theme.colors.disabledBackground` meets WCAG 4.5:1 contrast; if not, adjust disabled text color."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "The component uses `TouchableOpacity` which on Android adds opacity feedback, but does not match the spec's pressed color change.",
      "fix": "Switch to `Pressable` as noted above to control pressed styling."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "score": 6,
  "summary": "The sign-in screen is functional and clean but lacks visual polish and design depth. It meets basic usability needs but doesn't feel like a premium product. Typography is readable but lacks scale, spacing is minimal, and there's no visual hierarchy beyond the primary button. The layout is simple but unengaging, and the color scheme is flat with no brand identity.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "viewport": "phone",
      "issue": "No visual hierarchy or clear emphasis on the primary action beyond button color; the 'Log in' button is the only prominent element.",
      "fix": "Add subtle visual hierarchy: increase button size, use bold typography, add a drop shadow or rounded corners for depth, and space the button further from surrounding elements."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "viewport": "phone",
      "issue": "Typography lacks scale and variation; title, labels, and button text are all similar in weight and size, reducing visual interest.",
      "fix": "Establish a type scale: use a larger, bolder font for the title, medium for labels, and small for placeholder text. Use bold for button text to reinforce primary action."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "viewport": "phone",
      "issue": "Spacing is minimal and feels cramped; fields are too close to each other and to the edges, reducing perceived breathing room.",
      "fix": "Increase vertical spacing between fields and the title. Add padding around the form to create a centered, balanced layout."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "viewport": "phone",
      "issue": "Form fields are basic, unstyled inputs with no visual feedback or affordance beyond placeholder text.",
      "fix": "Add subtle borders or focus states. Consider rounded corners and a consistent stroke width for all inputs. Use placeholder text that’s slightly lighter or smaller than labels."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "viewport": "phone",
      "issue": "The 'Sign up' link is underlined and gray, but lacks visual separation from the button and the rest of the form, making it appear like a footnote.",
      "fix": "Style the link to match the button’s importance: use a similar color or add a subtle underline. Consider placing it above or below the button with more spacing."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "viewport": "phone",
      "issue": "The background is a flat, neutral gray, which feels generic and lacks brand identity.",
      "fix": "Use a brand color or gradient for the background. Add subtle texture or a branded illustration to enhance visual appeal."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "score": 7,
  "summary": "The sign-up screen is clean and functional, with clear visual hierarchy and a strong primary action. Typography is readable and consistent, spacing is generous, and the layout is well-aligned. However, it lacks polish in form design and visual depth, and the desktop version is underutilized. It’s good but not exceptional.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "viewport": "phone",
      "issue": "Password field lacks a visible character counter or validation indicator for password strength.",
      "fix": "Add a small indicator (e.g., progress bar or icon) that shows password strength as user types."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "viewport": "phone",
      "issue": "The 'Create account' button is large and prominent, but lacks a subtle shadow or elevation to create depth.",
      "fix": "Add a soft drop shadow or elevation to the button to make it feel more tactile and interactive."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "viewport": "phone",
      "issue": "The 'Already have an account? Log in' link is centered, but its text is not bolded or styled to match the primary action button.",
      "fix": "Make the link text bold or use a slightly darker color to visually connect it to the primary CTA."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "viewport": "desktop",
      "issue": "The desktop version is a stretched version of the phone layout, with no adaptation for larger screens (e.g., no columnar layout, no expanded fields).",
      "fix": "Adapt the desktop layout to use more horizontal space, perhaps with two columns for fields or larger input areas, to feel native to desktop."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "verdict": "revise",
  "issues": [
    "TypeScript error in `expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx`: the `TextInput` components use an invalid prop `accessibilityRole=\"textbox\"` (lines where the email and password fields are defined). Remove the `accessibilityRole` prop (or replace it with a valid role such as \"none\") to satisfy the `tsc` compiler.",
    "TypeScript error in `expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx`: the `TextInput` components also use `accessibilityRole=\"textbox\"` for the email and password fields. Remove this prop (or replace it with a valid role) to fix the compiler errors.",
    "TypeScript error in `expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx`: `FileSystem.cacheDirectory` is not defined in the Expo FileSystem type definitions. Replace the usage with a correctly typed property, e.g. `FileSystem.documentDirectory` or cast to `any` like `(FileSystem as any).cacheDirectory`, and adjust the import accordingly.",
    "UI primary‑flow test fails to fill the \"Email address\" field on the Sign‑Up screen. This is caused by the invalid accessibility role on the `TextInput` components, which makes the field not findable by the test harness. After removing the invalid `accessibilityRole` props, ensure the inputs retain `accessibilityLabel=\"Email address\"` (and similarly for password) and are focusable. Optionally add `accessible={true}` for extra safety."
  ],
  "feedback": "The backend passes all acceptance tests, but static validation fails due to TypeScript compilation errors, and the UI flow test cannot interact with the sign‑up form. Fix the accessibilityRole usage in the SignIn and SignUp screens, correct the FileSystem cacheDirectory reference in ExportScreen, and verify that the email/password inputs are properly accessible. Once these changes are applied and the UI flow test passes, the solution can be approved."
