{
  "verdict": "revise",
  "issues": [
    "The UI primary flow test fails because Playwright cannot locate and fill the \"Email address\" field on the Sign‑Up screen. The sign‑up form uses Unicode narrow‑no‑break spaces (U+202F) in the helper text (<Text style={styles.helper}>12 + characters, ...</Text>) which cause syntax errors during bundling and can prevent proper rendering of the component on the web. This results in the email input not being correctly associated with its label, so the locator times out. Fix the sign‑up screen by removing the problematic Unicode characters (use regular spaces) and ensure the TextInput has a proper `id`/`htmlFor` pairing and an explicit `aria-label` or `accessibilityLabel`. Also update the helper text to avoid non‑standard whitespace. After these changes the sign‑up page should render correctly and the primary flow test will be able to fill the email field and continue.",
  "feedback\": \"The backend passes its unit tests, but the Expo UI has a critical failure: the Sign‑Up form cannot be interacted with by the automated UI test, likely due to the Unicode whitespace in the helper Text causing a bundling/parsing error and breaking the label‑input association. Clean up the SignUpScreen component (remove the U+202F characters, confirm the label’s htmlFor matches the input’s id, and add a stable aria‑label) and re‑run the UI flow test. Once the primary flow passes, all checks will be green and the solution can be approved.\")"

  ]
}

